---A firewall defines the behavior of a firewall, the main VPC where the firewall is used, the Availability Zones where the firewall can be used, and one subnet to use for a firewall endpoint within each of the Availability Zones. The Availability Zones are defined implicitly in the subnet specifications.
---@class aws.network_firewall.Firewall
---@field FirewallName? aws.network_firewall.ResourceName The descriptive name of the firewall. You can't change the name of a firewall after you create it.
---@field FirewallArn? aws.network_firewall.ResourceArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the firewall.
---@field FirewallPolicyArn aws.network_firewall.ResourceArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the firewall policy.
---@field VpcId aws.network_firewall.VpcId The unique identifier of the VPC where the firewall is in use.
---@field SubnetMappings aws.network_firewall.SubnetMappings The primary public subnets that Network Firewall is using for the firewall. Network Firewall creates a firewall endpoint in each subnet. Create a subnet mapping for each Availability Zone where you want to use the firewall.
---@field DeleteProtection aws.network_firewall.Boolean A flag indicating whether it is possible to delete the firewall. A setting of TRUE indicates that the firewall is protected against deletion. Use this setting to protect against accidentally deleting a firewall that is in use. When you create a firewall, the operation initializes this flag to TRUE.
---@field SubnetChangeProtection aws.network_firewall.Boolean A setting indicating whether the firewall is protected against changes to the subnet associations. Use this setting to protect against accidentally modifying the subnet associations for a firewall that is in use. When you create a firewall, the operation initializes this setting to TRUE.
---@field FirewallPolicyChangeProtection aws.network_firewall.Boolean A setting indicating whether the firewall is protected against a change to the firewall policy association. Use this setting to protect against accidentally modifying the firewall policy for a firewall that is in use. When you create a firewall, the operation initializes this setting to TRUE.
---@field Description? aws.network_firewall.Description A description of the firewall.
---@field FirewallId aws.network_firewall.ResourceId The unique identifier for the firewall.
---@field Tags? aws.network_firewall.TagList
---@field EncryptionConfiguration? aws.network_firewall.EncryptionConfiguration A complex type that contains the Amazon Web Services KMS encryption configuration settings for your firewall.
---@field NumberOfAssociations? aws.network_firewall.NumberOfAssociations The number of VpcEndpointAssociation resources that use this firewall.
---@field EnabledAnalysisTypes? aws.network_firewall.EnabledAnalysisTypes An optional setting indicating the specific traffic analysis types to enable on the firewall.
---@field TransitGatewayId? aws.network_firewall.TransitGatewayId The unique identifier of the transit gateway associated with this firewall. This field is only present for transit gateway-attached firewalls.
---@field TransitGatewayOwnerAccountId? aws.network_firewall.AWSAccountId The Amazon Web Services account ID that owns the transit gateway. This may be different from the firewall owner's account ID when using a shared transit gateway.
---@field AvailabilityZoneMappings? aws.network_firewall.AvailabilityZoneMappings The Availability Zones where the firewall endpoints are created for a transit gateway-attached firewall. Each mapping specifies an Availability Zone where the firewall processes traffic.
---@field AvailabilityZoneChangeProtection aws.network_firewall.Boolean A setting indicating whether the firewall is protected against changes to its Availability Zone configuration. When set to TRUE, you must first disable this protection before adding or removing Availability Zones.
---@field NatGatewayCreateMappings? aws.network_firewall.NatGatewayCreateMappingsList The NAT gateways that you specified for Network Firewall to create for a proxy mode firewall. To get the IDs and status of the NAT gateways that are attached to the firewall, see NatGatewayAttachments in the firewall's SyncStates.
---@field ProxySettings? aws.network_firewall.ProxySettings The proxy settings of a proxy mode firewall: its listeners and, if you specified them, your own CertificateArn and DomainName.
---@field VpcEndpoint? aws.network_firewall.VpcEndpoint The VPC and subnets for the endpoints of a proxy mode firewall.
---@field TransparentFilteringNatScope? aws.network_firewall.TransparentFilteringNatScope How a proxy mode firewall handles traffic that isn't sent to its proxy listener. NAT_ALL sends this traffic out through the firewall's NAT gateway after inspection. NAT_NONE returns it to the firewall endpoint without address translation.

