---@field FirewallDefaultAction? aws.network_firewall.PolicyDefaultAction|string The action that the firewall engine takes on traffic that doesn't match any firewall engine rule at a hook. The firewall engine is drop by default. You can set the default action to one of the following:
---@field StatefulEngineOptions? aws.network_firewall.StatefulEngineOptionsV2 Additional options governing how the engines handle stateful traffic, such as the stream exception policy and flow timeouts.
---@field TLSInspectionConfigurationArn? aws.network_firewall.ResourceArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the TLS inspection configuration to use to decrypt traffic for inspection. Next Generation policies support session holding only. For more information, see Inspecting SSL/TLS traffic with TLS inspection configurations in the Network Firewall Developer Guide.
---@field PolicyVariables? aws.network_firewall.PolicyVariables Contains variables that you can use to override default Suricata settings in your Next Generation policy.
---@field Route53ResolvedIPValidation? aws.network_firewall.Route53ResolvedIPValidation The settings that enable resolved IP validation for the Next Generation policy. Resolved IP validation verifies that a connection's destination IP address is one that the Amazon Route 53 Resolver returned in a DNS response for a domain. A VPC that's associated with the Route 53 Resolver DNS Firewall rule group that you specify must send the response. This checks how the destination IP address was ...

