---@field ReferenceSets? aws.network_firewall.ReferenceSets The list of a rule group's reference sets. Firewall engine rule groups don't support IP set references (reference sets); this setting applies to IPS engine rule groups. To use CIDR ranges in firewall engine rules, use rule variables instead.

---@alias aws.network_firewall.FirewallRuleGroupEntries aws.network_firewall.FirewallRuleGroupEntry[]

---A single entry in the firewall section of a Next Generation policy. An entry either references an existing firewall engine rule group by ARN or embeds a rule group directly in the policy, and it carries the priority that sets the rule group's evaluation order within the firewall section.
---@class aws.network_firewall.FirewallRuleGroupEntry
---@field Priority? aws.network_firewall.Priority The priority of the rule group entry within the firewall section. Network Firewall evaluates the firewall section's entries in order of increasing priority value. Each entry in the firewall section must have a unique priority.
---@field ResourceArn? aws.network_firewall.ResourceArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of an existing firewall engine rule group to reference in this entry. Provide either ResourceArn to reference an existing rule group or InlineRuleGroup to embed a rule group in the policy.
---@field InlineRuleGroup? aws.network_firewall.FirewallRuleGroup A firewall engine rule group defined directly in the policy, instead of referenced by ARN. Provide either InlineRuleGroup to embed a rule group or ResourceArn to reference an existing rule group. An embedded rule group can't use a domain list rules source; to filter on a domain list, reference a standalone rule group by ARN instead.

